Usage: agent-deck try <name> [options]

Quick experiment: find or create a dated folder and start a session.

Arguments:
  <name>    Experiment name (fuzzy matched against existing experiments)

Options:
  -c string
    	AI tool to use (short)
  -cmd string
    	AI tool to use (defaults to config)
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -l	List experiments (short)
  -list
    	List experiments without creating session
  -no-session
    	Create folder only, don't start session
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output
  -sandbox
    	Run session in Docker sandbox

Examples:
  agent-deck try redis-cache          # Create/find redis-cache experiment
  agent-deck try rds                  # Fuzzy match 'redis-cache'
  agent-deck try --list               # List all experiments
  agent-deck try --list redis         # Fuzzy search experiments
  agent-deck try myproject -c gemini  # Use Gemini instead of Claude
  agent-deck try myproject --no-session  # Just create folder

Config (<SANDBOX_HOME>/.config/agent-deck/config.toml):
  [experiments]
  directory = "~/src/tries"    # Base directory for experiments
  date_prefix = true           # Add YYYY-MM-DD- prefix
  default_tool = "claude"     # Default AI tool
